      'This page introduces the articles filed under governance. Governance here means the rules a team agrees to follow, the person who decides when a rule applies, and the record that shows what was decided. An article in this category explains one rule, one decision or one review, and says who owns it.',
      'Start a governance article with the decision, not the background. State what was decided, on which date, and by whom. Then give the reason in one or two sentences, so a reader who disagrees knows which part to challenge. Link the rule to the document or page where it is kept.',
      'A rule that nobody can find does not govern anything. Each article should therefore point to the single page that holds the current version of the rule. When the rule changes, update that page first and the article second, and change the updated date of the article so readers can see which version they read.',
